#!/bin/zsh
# Tiers every changed file for the review skill: one Jev Choice per file over
# ignore / skim / deep, judged from the path, its line counts, and the head of
# its diff. Git supplies the counts and excerpts; only the tier is a judgment.
# Each file goes up in its own request because neighboring files in one state
# pull the answer around (46 of 104 tiers moved between batch layouts in
# testing), and eight requests run at once to keep a big diff under ten seconds.
# Usage: jev-tier [<git diff args>]
#   no args: working tree and index against HEAD, plus untracked files
#   JEV_TIER_LINES caps the diff excerpt per file (default 60)
#   JEV_TIER_JOBS sets how many requests run at once (default 8)
# Output: one line per file, `tier  confidence  path`, deep first.
set -eu
set -o pipefail

question='{"tier": {
  "type": "choice",
  "instructions": "Which review tier does the changed file described in `file` need? Judge from its path, its line counts, and the head of its diff.",
  "criteria": {
    "ignore": "Generated or machine-managed content such as lockfiles, snapshots, build output, vendored code, or config that a command verifies better than a reader. Not worth reading.",
    "skim": "Hand-written but low impact if wrong: docs, copy, small mechanical edits, renames, or a change that only mirrors one made elsewhere. Glance for surprises.",
    "deep": "Logic, state, data flow, contracts, auth, money, migrations, or concurrency. A mistake here breaks behavior. Read carefully."
  }
}}'

if [[ ${1:-} == --judge ]]; then
  out=$(jq -c '{file: .}' "$2" | jev "$question" \
    | jq -c --slurpfile f "$2" '{path: $f[0].path, tier: .tier.choice, confidence: .tier.confidence}')
  print -r -- "$out" > "$2.out"
  exit 0
fi

typeset -a args
if (( $# )); then args=("$@"); else args=(HEAD); fi
excerpt_lines=${JEV_TIER_LINES:-60}
jobs=${JEV_TIER_JOBS:-8}
if [[ -z ${TYPESAFE_API_KEY:-} ]]; then
  key=$(pass show typesafe-ai-api-key)
  export TYPESAFE_API_KEY=${key%%$'\n'*}
fi

tmp=$(mktemp -d)
trap 'rm -rf "$tmp"' EXIT
n=0

entry() {
  n=$(( n + 1 ))
  jq -cn --arg p "$1" --arg s "$2" --arg a "$3" --arg r "$4" --arg d "$5" \
    '{path: $p, status: $s, lines_added: ($a | tonumber? // 0), lines_removed: ($r | tonumber? // 0), diff_head: $d}' \
    > "$tmp/$n.json"
}

for line in "${(@f)$(git diff --name-status -M "${args[@]}")}"; do
  [[ -n $line ]] || continue
  parts=("${(@s:	:)line}")
  kind=${parts[1][1]}
  file=${parts[-1]}
  numstat=$(git diff --numstat -M "${args[@]}" -- "$file")
  numstat=${numstat%%$'\n'*}
  added=${numstat%%	*}
  removed=${${numstat#*	}%%	*}
  lines=("${(@f)$(git diff -M "${args[@]}" -- "$file")}")
  excerpt=${(F)lines[1,$excerpt_lines]}
  entry "$file" "$kind" "$added" "$removed" "$excerpt"
done

if (( $# == 0 )); then
  for file in "${(@f)$(git ls-files --others --exclude-standard)}"; do
    [[ -n $file ]] || continue
    added=$(wc -l < "$file" | tr -d ' ')
    lines=("${(@f)$(<"$file")}")
    excerpt=${(F)lines[1,$excerpt_lines]}
    entry "$file" "untracked" "$added" 0 "$excerpt"
  done
fi

(( n )) || { print -u2 'jev-tier: no changed files'; exit 0; }

print -rl -- "$tmp"/*.json | xargs -P "$jobs" -n1 "$0" --judge \
  || { print -u2 'jev-tier: some files got no answer'; exit 1; }

cat "$tmp"/*.out | jq -rs '
  sort_by((if .tier == "deep" then 0 elif .tier == "skim" then 1 else 2 end), .path)
  | .[] | "\(.tier)\t\(.confidence * 100 | round / 100)\t\(.path)"' | column -t -s $'\t'
